.title AFE 16ch -- diode-OR soft-max threshold (xlse), delta = 0
* Generated by analog/AFE/scripts/gen_afe16.py -- do not hand-edit.
* Per-channel chain identical to AFE_tuning/netlists/v15_channel.cir.
* New vs the existing board: the comparator reference only (see below).

.include ../models/OPA379.LIB
* BAT54 as a 2-terminal .model: the vendor subckt carries a parametric
* 'mfg=' that ngspice rejects. Same params the verified netlists use.
.model Dbat54wt1 D(Is=2.2n Rs=2 N=1.03 Cjo=10p M=0.4 Vj=0.4 Bv=30
+ Ibv=10u Eg=0.69 Xti=2)

* ---- supplies -------------------------------------------------------
Vpos  vpos  0  DC 1.8
Vmid  vmid  0  DC 0.9        $ bias rail

* ---- microphone + preamp (G = 1 + Rf/Rg = 10) -----------------------
* Tone BURST (on 20-60 ms, off after) so the transient shows both the
* attack and the decay. u() is ngspice's unit step.
Bmic  vmic  vmid  V = 0.00252*sin(6.283185307*1349*time)
+ *(u(time-20m)-u(time-60m))
XUPRE vmic  npre  vpos 0 vin  OPA379
Rf    vin   npre  90k
Rg    npre  vmid  10k

* ---- shared threshold generator (THE NEW PART) ----------------------
* xmax variant: an IDEAL max(), which is what the diode-OR would be
* if n*V_T were zero. Not buildable as written -- it exists to isolate
* what the LSE floor T*ln(16) is worth. See SPICE_FINDINGS.md 2.
Bmax  v_max 0  V = max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(v(ve0),v(ve1)),v(ve2)),v(ve3)),v(ve4)),v(ve5)),v(ve6)),v(ve7)),v(ve8)),v(ve9)),v(ve10)),v(ve11)),v(ve12)),v(ve13)),v(ve14)),v(ve15))

* C) V_ref, the low end of every divider. Training fixes it at the
*    envelope quiescent, i.e. delta = 0 (docs/EXPERIMENT_MAP.md A-3).
*
*    Kept as an ideal source on purpose, so delta is one sweepable knob
*    here exactly as floor_frac is in training. On the board it is a
*    divider off the 1.8 V rail through a unity-gain OPA379; the buffer
*    is NOT optional, because at quiescent D2 is reverse biased and the
*    envelope node is high impedance -- unbuffered, the 16 dividers drew
*    ~0.9 uA and moved the reference 40 mV.
*
*    A replica detector was tried first and does not work. Its R4 has to
*    sit at the filter output DC level, not at vmid, and that level is
*    itself 2 op-amp offsets below vmid. Worse, the quiescent envelope is
*    da + (R5/R4)*(vf - da): each channel's own offset, amplified 4.7x,
*    random per device. Nothing passive tracks that, so a replica buys
*    less than it costs (3 op-amps) and this is a bring-up trim instead.
.param VREFSET=0.9183840   $ delta = +0.0 mV
Vref  v_ref 0  DC {VREFSET}

* ==== channel 0: f_c 166 Hz, Q 1.33, alpha 0.8745 ====
R1_0   vin    np0   16.5064k
C1_0   vmid   np0   76.5554n
RA1_0  c2p0 np0   12.3353k
XU1_0  np0  nn0   vpos 0 vf0  OPA379
C2_0   c2p0 nn0   76.5554n
RA2_0  nn0  vf0   12.3353k
R2_0   nu20 vf0   100k
R3_0   vmid   nu20  100k
XU2_0  nu20 nn0   vpos 0 c2p0  OPA379
R4_0   vf0  da0   10k
R5_0   da0  ve0   47k
R6_0   vmid   np30  8.25k
D1_0   da0  dk0   Dbat54wt1
XU3_0  np30 da0   vpos 0 dk0  OPA379
D2_0   dk0  ve0   Dbat54wt1
C3_0   ve0  0       100n
DOR_0  ve0  v_or    Dbat54wt1
Ra_0   v_max  vt0   125.5000k
Rb_0   vt0  v_ref   874.5000k
Bcmp_0 vo0  0  V = 0.9 + 0.9*tanh(2e4*(v(ve0) - v(vt0)))

